# Git LFS.
#
# The Rectangle's rendered narration — 24 wavs, ~46MB — is committed rather
# than regenerated, because it is the take the talk was TIMED against. Every
# **DURATION:** marker in NARRATION.md is measured off these exact files, so a
# clone that re-renders instead of fetching gets a script whose timings
# describe audio it does not have. Derived, yes; reproducible byte-for-byte,
# no.
#
# LFS rather than plain git because 46MB of binary would sit in every clone's
# history forever, and re-cutting the script rewrites all 24.
#
# What is deliberately NOT here:
#
#   voices/  — 224MB of piper's models. Third-party, downloaded by say.sh on
#              first run, and not ours to redistribute.
#   .txt     — the receipts beside each wav. Small, text, and diffable, and
#              they are what present.py compares to decide a take is stale;
#              in LFS a fresh clone could not run that check without fetching.
#
# CI does not fetch these. actions/checkout defaults to lfs:false, so its
# working copy has pointer files — which is correct, because nothing in the
# build or the test suite reads presentations/.
presentations/the-rectangle/audio/*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
